     {
      "start": 1903,
      "end": 1920,
      "headway_min": 420,
      "note": "Chartered 10 January 1899 by George C. Sturgiss and built in three phases from Morgantown: the first phase, Morgantown out along Deckers Creek through Sabraton, Dellslow and Masontown to Bretz, opened in September 1903. Stephen B. Elkins bought the company in 1902. Independent operation ended when the Baltimore & Ohio leased the M&K in 1920 (buying it outright in 1922). Frequency estimated, unsourced.",
      "sources": [
       "Segment-level: the phase opening dates, the 1899 charter, the Elkins purchase and the 1920 B&O lease are from the Wikipedia article on the M&K and from WVNC Rails; the headway is an estimate and is not sourced.",
