      "start": 1906,
      "end": 1920,
      "headway_min": 420,
      "note": "Chartered 10 January 1899 by George C. Sturgiss and built in three phases from Morgantown: the second phase, Bretz through Reedsville to Kingwood, opened in March 1906; by that year the line was running two passenger trains a day to Kingwood. Stephen B. Elkins bought the company in 1902. Independent operation ended when the Baltimore & Ohio leased the M&K in 1920 (buying it outright in 1922). Frequency estimated, unsourced.",
